WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.501
-Welcome back. We're talking to Madonna, everybody.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.934
Her album

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:07.701
"Finally Enough Love: 50 Number Ones"

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.234
is out August 19th.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.767
How is the -- How is the family, by the way?

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.200
How's my man Dave?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.968
-Your man Dave is alright, you know?

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.067
He's a -- First of all, he's a huge fan of yours.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.634
-I love -- I'm a fan of Dave.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:21.300
-He's so jealous that I'm sitting next to you right now.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.701
I think he was going to come here tonight,

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:25.100
but he had a boxing lesson today.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.100
-Is he boxing? -Dave, are you here?

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.767
No, he's not here. -No, he's not here.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.234
David?!

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.801
-Dave! -Dave!

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.634
Tell him I said hi, will you, please?

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.868
-You know, he makes music now, too.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.367
He's gonna end up being one of your guests.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.067
-He is, right? He's got something.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.434
He's got "it." -Something?

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.701
-Yeah, he's got "it." He's got magic. He's funny.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.367
He's charming. He's athletic.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.767
He's a good-looking dude.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.100
-He can put on any outfit and look swag as you know what.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.501
-Yeah. -It's really irritating.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:50.934
-Does he ever give you feedback?

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.267
-He wears my clothes and looks better in them.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.834
-How does he -- -He can even wear a dress

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.033
and look butch.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.100
Ooh. Speaking of butch...

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.067
I got a present for you. -What?

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.334
-It's a little handbag and it says "butch."

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.501
-For real?

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:08.767
-Yeah, put it on. -Look at this.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.601
-You got to put it around -- put it around your neck.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:11.767
-Let me just see it. This is --

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.100
-Let me just show you how to do it.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.334
-You know, I have one of these already.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.167
-Do you? -No, of course not.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.167
-Put your arm through it. -Oh, my gosh.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:22.567
This is -- -There you go.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.300
-That's it right there. Should I wear this?

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.934
Are you kidding me?

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.667
-You got swag.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.701
-I think this is so -- this is so cool.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:38.000
I found like -- -You can put your coins in it.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.400
-Yeah, my MetroCard. I'll fold up my MetroCard.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.133
Put it in there. I go, "I'm sorry, guys.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.634
I've got to get in the subway."

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:44.801
-Yeah, you can put your --

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.634
-"Watch out. Butch is coming through!

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:47.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.133
You guys met Butch?"

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:52.834
♪♪

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.234
I love this. I am honored. Thank you for this.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.901
Oh, my gosh. I'm going to treasure this.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.400
I'll wear this all the time. Yes!

00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:59.701
-You're lying.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.100
-You know, there's so many artists on this thing.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.501
I was looking through it. I'm like --

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:06.234
We know a lot of people. Britney Spears is on this one.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:09.667
Timberlake. Nicki Minaj.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:11.434
Are there any -- -Nile Rodgers.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.667
-Nile Rodgers, of course. The one and only.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:15.701
Are there any people that you go like,

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.534
"I think eventually I want to do something with them,"

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.601
or you haven't done that you want to?

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.767
-I mean, there's one artist that I worship

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.868
more than anything in life and I would love to collaborate

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.267
with him, and that's Kendrick Lamar.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.033
-Well. Yeah. Wow. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:29.701
I thought you were gonna say -- -His new record is --

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.834
His new record is, like, history-making.

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.200
-It is unbelievable, right?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.801
-Mind-bogglingly brilliant, yeah.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.067
It's insane. Have you had him on your show yet?

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.801
-Yeah. He is mind-boggling.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.434
He's brilliant. -So talented.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:44.067
-You -- You brought up something when we were doing

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:45.601
our bit -- you said maybe you want to do this.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.067
And I don't know if you still want to do it.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.634
-What? Host your show? -No.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.567
You said you wanted to play this thing with me where we --

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.701
-Yeah, I want to play all kinds of games with you.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:57.167
But for now -- I told you. Seduction.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.067
-But you have -- -Okay. "Finally Enough Love."

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:01.901
-This is every letter of the alphabet on these cards.

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.200
Okay? And you -- you wanted -- -That's 26.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.634
He didn't know it at the time.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:08.634
-I knew it was in the 20s.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.834
But you wanted me to shuffle this around,

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:13.701
and then we'll pick one and then just say the first word

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.767
that comes to our mind and then analyze each other?

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.868
-Yeah, well, this is how we get to know each other,

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:20.801
and also the audience can get to know one --

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.901
you know, you, more importantly.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.634
They already know everything about me.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:27.100
-I think this is a good idea. -But have you shuffled them?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.334
-No. -I think we should.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.868
-I will shuffle them.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:33.167
-So, should we -- But I need to take 13 for myself.

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.467
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.267
-I'm not doing 13 letters of the alphabet.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.534
The show is only an hour long.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:40.033
-...5, 6, 7, 8, 9. Make it longer.

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.300
10, 11...

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.367
-I'm not making the show longer. -12, 13. Why not?

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.834
-I don't know. -It should be.

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:46.434
It's fun. I'm fun.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.567
-You are more than fun. Alright. Who goes first?

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.267
-Okay, this is a psychoanalytic game.

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.067
And so what we're going to do is turn the card over.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.334
And I'll go first.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.968
And whatever comes to my mind, I'm going to say the word.

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.868
I'm just going to blurt it right out.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.634
-Okay. And then -- -So be brave.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:04.534
-Yes. -Don't censor yourself.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:05.901
And I'm not going to, either.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.334
-Go. -For once.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:08.667
-Okay.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.834
-Oh, my God. I got a P. [Bleep]

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:17.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.434
I knew that was gonna happen! -What in the world?!

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:22.434
Out of all the letters in the alphabet.

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.234
-Yeah, but -- -How in the world --

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.734
-The universe wanted me to get that letter.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:26.968
Your turn.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.734
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.467
This is insane, by the way.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:33.000
♪♪

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.400
Jimmy.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.968
-Ohh.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.834
My favorite song on the "True Blue" album.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.667
-You think that's about you, don't you?

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.434
-"Jimmy, Jimmy" is about me, yeah.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.501
That's bizarre, by the way. We just picked --

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:45.834
-You get the safe letters. -Yeah.

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.901
-Okay. I'm next.

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:50.834
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:53.100
Revolting.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.701
-What's revolting? -Ignorance.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:57.968
-Yeah.

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.701
[ Applause ]

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:02.000
-Think about it. I just went deep.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.167
I went there. I like that sound.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:07.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:08.767
Go for it.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.634
-I mean, if I don't say "xylophone,"

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:12.901
I'm going to say "Madame X."

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.300
-Oh, God. -What else am I going to say?

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.167
-X-rated.

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:20.234
-Yeah. Of course. Yeah. Of course I went to xylophone.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.667
That's why we -- [ Laughter ]

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.601
-That's why you get paid the medium bucks.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.734
-That's why you get paid the big b-- the medium bucks.

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:28.968
I'm stealing that. That's funny.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.534
Alright. Go.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.834
♪♪

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:34.133
-Hoe!

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:40.901
-What in the world is going on? -I'm sorry.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.734
-God keeps giving me these provocative letters.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:46.868
♪♪

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:48.334
-This is unbelievable.

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:49.968
-You're doing this on purpose. -I swear I'm not.

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:51.434
This is all random. Look at all these.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.734
These are all random letters. I'm not doing this on purpose.

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:55.467
-How do we even know? You're David Blaine.

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:57.234
-Let's just do the -- Let's do the last one.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.801
-Well, you didn't say the -- what comes to mind.

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:02.133
-The one and only, Madonna, of course comes to mind.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.767
What are you talking about? What am I supposed to do?

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:09.200
Think of another one? Mom? Mommy? Mommy?!

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.901
You want me to break down -- -Yeah.

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:12.067
-And talk -- -Cry.

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:14.067
-[Voice breaking] And talk about my childhood?

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:18.267
I promised myself I wouldn't do it. Not here.

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:20.167
[Normal voice] Alright, ready?

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.934
-Wait. Is this the last one? God. Time goes by so fast.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.467
-Why don't we do one

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:27.167
and we both say the same word at the same time?

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:28.868
No matter what it is. -Okay.

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:34.167
[ Drum roll ]

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:35.634
Oh, no.

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:39.868
Oh, what?

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.334
Z--

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:44.300
-Zebra.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.767
Wait. Z?

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:48.501
Zelda. -Xylophone?

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:49.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:52.334
-Can make it an "N." "Xylophone."

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:53.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.667
-That's the worst letter. -It's the worst letter.

00:06:55.667 --> 00:06:57.367
-It should be at the end. -Ready?

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:58.834
-Yes.

00:06:58.834 --> 00:07:00.434
[ Drum roll ]

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.667
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:06.434 --> 00:07:07.634
-Wet. -Winner.

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:08.901
Okay. Alright, alright.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:11.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:17.300
♪♪

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.801
-[Bleep] happens.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:24.133
I'm sorry.

00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:25.501
Temptations. -Tattle tale.

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:26.834
Okay.

00:07:26.834 --> 00:07:28.601
-My words are better than yours.

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:29.968
-They are.

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:32.901
-You're so PG.

00:07:32.901 --> 00:07:34.400
Idiot! -Icon.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:43.634 --> 00:07:45.601
Madonna, everybody!

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:48.701
"Finally Enough Love: 50 Number Ones"

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.467
is available August 19th.

00:07:50.467 --> 00:07:52.701
Elvis Costello joins us after the break.

00:07:52.701 --> 00:07:54.300
Stick around, everybody!

